{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And YHWH Elohim formed.</b> To be sure, for the coming-to-be of living creatures this was not sufficient; rather, the formation by the Creator, blessed be He, proceeded through varying modes — for the formation of man He selected from the dust of the earth a more honored portion than it." "<b>And He breathed into his nostrils the breath of life.</b> A vital soul prepared to receive the image of Elohim, as it says: וְנִשְׁמַת שַׁדַּי תְּבִינֵם (Job 32:8). Nevertheless, <b>and the man became a living soul</b> — despite all this, he was merely a living creature, not speaking, until he was created in image and likeness."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:38.966227552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}